; Call-position [and ...]/[or ...] are desugared before scope information
; exists, so they are effectively SPECIAL FORMS: a local binding named
; `and`/`or` cannot shadow them at call sites (every backend agrees). This
; is a deliberate language decision that came with making them short-circuit.
[fn main []
  [let and [fn [a b] 42]]
  [println [and 1 2]]
  [let or [fn [a b] 43]]
  [println [or false 9]]]
